Programmers use the term "environment" much like it's used in
everyday speech.  It's all the tools and techniques
you use to do your work.

Install the cygwin tools.
Make a directory to do your first project in.
Put a .c file called main.c in that directory containing:

#include <stdio.h>
int main() {
  printf("Hello\n");
  return 0;
}

Then put a "Makefile" in the same directory.
Use the name "Makefile".

In the Makefile put:

all: main
main: main.c
      gcc main.c -o main
test: main
      ./main         

Make sure you use tabs for the whitespace shown
for the makefile.

Then in the same directory type:

make
and/or
make test

Now you have an environment.


